# scripts/inline-content.js renames a few things to <name>.parked for the
# duration of a deploy — the content file, once it's inside index.html, and the
# local dev toolbar. Matching the suffix rather than the real paths is
# deliberate: `wrangler dev` honours this file too, so listing a real path here
# would also stop the local server serving it, which is where both of those are
# needed. Parking only exists between the inline and the revert.
# data/legal.json is untouched: it's fetched on demand when a policy page opens,
# so it isn't part of first paint and stays a file of its own.
*.parked
.backups
# Source art kept in the repo so it can be re-encoded, never served — each has
# a .webp beside it that is what the site actually links to.
#
# The two static faces are here for the same reason: scripts/subset-font.py
# cuts fonts/dmsans-{500,700}-{core,ext}.woff2 from them, and those are what
# @font-face points at. A .ttf is uncompressed, so uploading one would put a
# 56 KB file on the edge that nothing links to and that is nearly four times
# the size of the .woff2 built from it.
#
# OFL.txt is not a source and is not served either, but it stays in the repo:
# the SIL Open Font License requires the licence and copyright notice to
# accompany any redistributed or modified copy of the font, and the subset
# .woff2 files are exactly that.
fonts/DM_Sans/static/DMSans-Medium.ttf
fonts/DM_Sans/static/DMSans-Bold.ttf
fonts/DM_Sans/OFL.txt
# The 404 animation's source. scripts/resize-images.js converts it to
# images/404.webp, which is what the page links to — a third of the bytes for
# the same 33 frames.
images/404.gif
images/pfp.png
images/work/caseystevenson/caseystevenson.png
images/work/northbound-gear/northbound-gear-logo.png
images/work/northbound-gear/northbound-gear-beaniedesign.png
README.md
wrangler.jsonc
